# POST /ipp/provision — step 0: who may call it.
#
# The route is open on loopback (the demo) and closed the moment a password
# is set: `txco auth tenant secrets set IPP_PROVISION_PASSWORD --tenant
# <slug>`, then callers send `curl -u provision:<password>`. The secret never
# reaches the envelope: txco://basic-auth-verify consumes it inside the op
# and emits only a verdict (@computed.basic_auth_ok). `allow_unconfigured =
# true` is the DECISION, written here where it can be seen: unset ⇒ open.
# The reject rule in 095 fires on anything but an explicit true, so the
# route fails CLOSED on a chassis without this op. (imap-hello's 090 says
# the same at more length.)
#
# This is the password of the PROVISIONING ROUTE, not of any printer. A
# printer has no password of its own: see 120/credential.txcl.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.method == "POST" && @web.req.url.path == "/ipp/provision"
WITH user = "provision",
     secrets.password.secret = "IPP_PROVISION_PASSWORD",
     secrets.password.optional = true,
     allow_unconfigured = true
  EXEC "txco://basic-auth-verify"
